  "prompt": "You are the coding agent of the imports team. You can use the tools provided.\n\nIssue #412: invoice imports crash on dates such as \"2026/03/05\" and \"05.03.2026\" (day first). Fix the issue. Then write pr.json with \"summary\" (one sentence), \"ci_status\" (\"green\" or \"red\", from your last test run) and \"failing_tests\" (a list, empty if none). When you are done, reply with a short summary.",
  "final_response": "I have fixed the issue where `parse_date` crashed on dates using slashes or dotted day-first formats. I updated the `split_date` helper to normalize separators and correctly identify the year regardless of whether it appears at the start or the end of the string. All tests now pass.\n\nSummary of changes:\n- Modified `app/parser.py` to handle `/` and `.` as date separators.\n- Added logic to detect the position of the year to support both ISO-like and day-first formats.\n- Verified the fix with `tests/test_parser.py`.",
